PX30: do not build the open TPL when binman uses Rockchip's DDR binary.

U-Boot 2025.10 already supports ROCKCHIP_EXTERNAL_TPL in rockchip-u-boot.dtsi.
PX30's unconditional select is the only change needed to let that path omit
an in-tree TPL. Keep the original selection when no external TPL is requested.
No SRAM limits, DRAM timings, or hardware registers are changed.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ config ROCKCHIP_PX30
 	select SUPPORT_SPL
 	select SUPPORT_TPL
 	select SPL
-	select TPL
+	select TPL if !ROCKCHIP_EXTERNAL_TPL
 	select TPL_TINY_FRAMEWORK if TPL
 	select TPL_HAVE_INIT_STACK if TPL
 	imply SPL_SEPARATE_BSS
